A||||47||Voytek||Whipped by an MR2||||9||
Z||000000||Voytek||05-29-2001||03:15 PM||||Ok.  This was a bit embarrasing but it sure made me wonder about MR2's.  So I'm on my way to work the other day.  I get to a light in the left lane and the right lane ends about 200 m past the light.  Next to me is a sports bike revving his engine (I'm thinking I'll be nice and let him slip in front of me).  Behind the bike I see a later model MR2.  Looked really nice in my right mirror.  Since I'm usually not that nice to rice, I figure it's time to show him what my recently (4000 km) rebuilt 3.1 can do (I mean, after all, I DO have a performance cam, no cat and headers, right?).  So the light changes.  The bike is gone, err... I mean I let him in front of me.  As I beat the crap out of my car and shift like a maniac, the MR2 is disappearing from my rear view mirror.  The weird thing is, it's not getting smaller, but rather it seems to be passing me!  As we get towards the end of the 2-lane stretch and doing about 100 kph (60 mph), Mister 2 suddenly rockets past me to at least about 140 / 150 kph!  My eyes just about popped out of my head!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> The MR2 had absolutely no stickers or decals on it but I figured it must have been a turbo.  Well, it turns out the guy goes to my gym.  The car has ONLY a 2.0 L 4-banger with a tweeked up turbo, intercooler and free flowing exhaust (and a couple of other small things I can't remember).  WOW.  I NEED A TURBO!!!!!!!!!!!!!!  (and about $4000 CDN)  Please e-mail me if you'd like to contribute to my cause.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||05-29-2001||03:18 PM||||yep! a turbo can double the HP on an engine, while adding only about 10 lbs to the cars weight.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Toddster||05-29-2001||03:24 PM||||Voytek, Your financial problem can be solved as I recently did by visiting my local Pick&Pull wrecking yard. I found a 90 Grand Prix with a 3.1 turbo. I pulled the turbo, hoses, intercooler, crossover pipe, etc. It all bolts right up to the stock 2.8 fiero motor. All I need now is an MSD ignition for the advance, a custom exhaust, and a new computer chip. All the parts from the wrecking yard cost $100 total! For another $500 I can get the rest of the stuff I need to convert the GT into a Kickemus-maximus-ricebuttamus machine.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Voytek||05-29-2001||03:51 PM||||WOW!  100 bucks, eh?  I might have to look around, in that case.  Do you need a new chip if a turbo is installed?<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||05-29-2001||04:07 PM||||the car ran 5.9 to sixty stock and high 14's. It should have beat you. a few little mods on a turbo make a big diffference. An adjustable boost valve made with  a fish tank valve for $15 can add 30-40 Hp. Or go to turbo city and get a boost valve for $45 , adjustable knob , just turn it for more power.<P>Those cars make 220hp Stock , your 3.1 makes probably under 200 (165-175) . With simple mods he could have 280hp No problem.<BR>Plus he weighs the same.<P>As for the turbo , you can get a new chip or a rising rate fuel press regulator. I would go with a Design One kit , or follow Dennis Lagrua's home grown turbo page and consult him. He built a good T3 turbo system for under $1000 US.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||05-29-2001||05:22 PM||||Those turbocharged MR2's are awesome sports cars. I wish I had one.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||RRobinson||05-29-2001||05:36 PM||||Hey Voytek, you would have to be really lucky to find a Grand Prix turbo 3.1 around here because a)they were only made for one year (1990) and b)there weren't any exported to Canada. <BR>Sadly, two of my favorite turbos weren't sold here either, I am referring of course to the mighty '91 GMC Syclone and the '92 and '93 Typhoon. Oh well...<BR>RR||||reg||1
Z||000007||Slammed Fiero||05-29-2001||06:39 PM||||There are a few typhoons / cyclones floating around Toronto. I saw one for sale in the TO Star a few months ago $25K canadian. There going for 15-18 US for a good example<P>I have seen 3.1ltr turbo Grand Am's is that the same motor as the prix?<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000008||firstfiero||05-29-2001||06:44 PM||||    Don't feel bad those 2nd gens our world beaters. To fast for their own good actually! Part of what led to their demise. High insurance rates killed them.  <P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Toddster||05-29-2001||07:34 PM||||Yeah, a new computer chip is a must. The stock computer in your car is GM's C3 ECM. It is designed for a car under normal aspiration. It's digital MAP has no allowance for how to behave under boost conditions. Hence you need to get a new chip programmed to tell your control devices (ie, throttle body, fuel injectors, etc) what to do. There are a couple of companies out there that sell them for about $150. Arizona Speed and Marine does one they are at 1-602-437-2510.<P>Timing advance is best handled externally by simply using an MSD ignition system designed for turbo applications. I'll try to get you the part number.<P>Also, regarding the scarcity of Turbo 3.1 engines. Yes, they are harder to find than your bare bones variety 3.1, They only made 2000 of them in 1989. But it became a regular production model in 1990 and many more were made. They rated 205 hp in stock trim, under-rated if you did very minor tinkering.<P>If finding one is too difficult, you can try to scavange a turbo from a Mitsubishi Galant or other turbo model. They have very nice turbos with cooling lines and oil lines. You need to custom fabricate a lot of plumbing but they work great and Pick&Pull sells 'em for just $40 each, in working order! I've got 3 or 4 just for spares.<P>There are other odds and ends you'll need too. Slammed Fiero makes a good suggestion by referring you to Dennis LaGru's web page. <p>[This message has been edited by Toddster (edited 05-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||KRMFiero||05-29-2001||09:30 PM||||MR2's may be faster, but Fiero's still have better looks<P>Well... the new 2001 MR2 : <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">rools:: i want, i want!||||reg||1
Z||000011||drednot||05-29-2001||09:34 PM||||Man 88formula, you love giving it up for the rice!  Your car is sooo much cooler than ANY MR2 ever made!  RICE~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000012||spideyfoot||05-30-2001||01:58 AM||||Play nice and open your eyes. The 2nd gen Mr2 is a great looking car so is the 3rd gen RX7 / 240,260,280zs/ The latest Supra/... Ok I like almost all 2 seater rear wheel drive cars with standards. I mean I'm hooked on the Fiero but I'm not going to dog a wicked car. That's where ricers came from Jap bikes whipping Harley ass they had nothing to beat the Bikes with so they went straight with patriotism. Sure our bikes leak oil, are slow, overheat, but hey they are built in the USA. So you should enjoy what rare cars they ship us because we sure don't buy them enough to warrant their exporting them. That's why the hot ones stay in Japan ( a stock Skyline would smoke 99.9% of this forum) So enjoy the fact that when you drive down the road you can be unique and have a car that is rarely seen, (doubly so in great condition ) and appreciate people with the same taste in sports cars. Some folks are reminding me of the new batch of upwardly mobile Harley snobs who turn their nose at me when I wave to them from my "rice rocket"<BR>I guess you take off your suit and tie put on a dewrag so you feel you have long hair and zamo your a bad ass outlaw biker.||||reg||1
