Z||000022||FLASHY||05-30-2001||04:42 PM||||85blackgt: Are you sure you're not talking about racing the mid 80's MR2 (non-turbo)? Those are no problem to beat. Voytek's talking about a '93 MR2 turbo that's been beefed a bit. Trust me, Voytek knows how to race. And if you ARE talking about beating the early 90's MR2 turbos then maybe THEY didn't know how to race. My brother owns a '93 MR2 non-turbo and it's a very very close race with my fiero GT. Once you add the turbo and upgrade a few parts that Mister 2 will fly right by.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>Voytek: If you can find two turbos and squeeze both in there I'll help you in a flash! Otherwise, I'll take one off your hands and make use of it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000023||Slammed Fiero||05-30-2001||06:01 PM||||Ahh ..it's a close race between your brothers 93 non turbo and your Fiero GT? is your car an auto?<P>The only reason I ask is that I havea  friend with a yellow 94 Non turbo and even when my car was stock I could beat it quite easily. It runs mid 16's int he 1/4. My friends 88 SC MR2 is a far better match.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
