Z||000028||FLASHY||05-30-2001||07:57 PM||||My brother has an '85 MR2 as well but it's nothing compared to his '93. I drove an '85 Super Charged and that was quite impressive.<P>I'm not saying I like them better than my Fiero that's for sure, but I think they deserve a bit more credit than people like to give them. Especially the 2nd gen ones. It's interesting how there are different opinions on the power comparrison. I don't want to start a fight or anything and I don't think there is one starting, just stating my experience that's all.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000029||88formula||05-30-2001||08:35 PM||||Drednot, what are you prejudice or something? What the hell is rice anyway? Define rice? You need to get with the time’s buddy because there is no such thing as a purely built American car anymore. <P>Here is some performance numbers to help clear things up here. <P>model and year....0-60...quarter mile<BR>88 MR2 SC.........7.0....15.3<BR>88 Fiero Formula..8.0....16.0<BR>86 Fiero GT.......8.0....16.3<BR>93 MR2 Turbo......6.1....14.7<BR>91 MR2 NA.........8.5....16.3<BR>84 Fiero 4........10.9...17.9 and then the rod blows out the side of the block. <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 05-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000030||Slammed Fiero||05-30-2001||08:57 PM||||I don't really trust "Road test #'s" Considering BanditBalz's Stock GT is a second faster than the ones listed in the stats above. and my basically stock 86 GT (cold air induction and a accel coil) posts 1+ sec faster to sixty (I have yet to drag it). perhaps the 86 GT listed in the stats is a 5spd. But even then I have seen 88 formulas post 15.5 sec 1/5 mile times.<P>A little Mr2 history.<P>85 Cars are the lightest , while the car looks the same as the 88-89 SC cars , the 85 Mr2 weighs 500lbs Plus less than the later cars. 85's weighed in at 2275-2300lbs.<P>The car got heavier year after year. The 88 SC Mr2's weight is on par with a Fiero GT's. mid 2700-low 2800lbs depending on options.<P>A well setup MR2 is a more nimble car than a Fiero , it is tighter as stated above ,it should be it's Toyota. <P>rice doesn't  refer to a type of car , rather a lifestyle that started in California. I have lots of Friends who drive imports (hondas and such) that are as serious as any of us are about there cars, there not ricers.<P>If you compare #'s from roadtests to real life you will come to the conclusion that logically the fastest stock Fiero should be an 85 GT 4spd. Notch back means lighter than the FB GT's 4spds, and the 4spd Muncie has the best gearing for drag racing/ competition.<P> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000031||Fiero5||05-30-2001||09:07 PM||||Well, let me speak up for my fellow 4 banger brother and sisters out there. I agree that the newer MR2's are really nice, and they can hang with the best of the hot rod big boys too. Those suckers are quick and with some impressive top end too!<P>I have burned many ricers including more ealier MR2's than have ever burned me. I did it for years with Fiero1, many, many times last year with Fiero5 and a few times allready this year with both Fiero1 and Fiero9. What is really so impressive about all this is? These are All 4 bangers.<P>OK, we own a bunch of V6 GT's too that have all torn up their share of ricers as well, but there is no better feeling than doing it with a sweet 4 banger Fiero!<P>I have found that taking out the muffler and adding large dual exhaust helps with the pick up off the line, as well as, blasting down the highway when you are doing 70+ and then want that quick extra fast surge up into the 100 mark.<P>The iron duke seems to always get it's fare share of bashing critics, but I won't make any excuses for any of my 4 bangers that can give me this kind of very impressive performance AND awesome gas mileage to boot!<P>Just my fact based two pennies on the subject.<P>Steve<BR>------------------<P>The First 6 Kelley Fieros<P>------------------<BR>                         <IMG SRC="http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/files/dads87GT.jpg">                       <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||6
Z||000032||drednot||05-30-2001||09:25 PM||||Well 88formula, If you like MR2's soooo much, why don't you just sell your Fieros and buy yourself a nice 93 MR2?  <P>BTW- Rice is a Jap car that LOOKS fast but is actualy not. Civic w body kit or any MR2 for example.  Those numbers meen nothing to me unless I see the timeslips to go with em.<BR>||||reg||10
